  "reasoning": [
    {
      "area": "AX hint policy and coalescing",
      "assessment": "Only chromeWindow (kAXFocusedWindowChangedNotification) revokes. Ordinary editor focus, ambiguous title changes and window creation do not revoke. A pending window-change reason cannot be overwritten by any later non-revoking hint in the same coalesced burst. needsWindowRefresh remains independent and OR-accumulated. Hints grant no input authority and read no titles, values or page text."
    },
    {
      "area": "Revoke before blocking AX refresh",
      "assessment": "The scheduled MainActor task checks task/generation/observer/process continuity, consumes pending reason and refresh flag, then invokes onChange synchronously before observeFocusedWindow. App requestArm clears old ACK/frozen press and rotates scheduler epoch synchronously. Only after that can the remote AX focused-window query block. The post-callback generation/observer guard prevents refresh if callback replaced or stopped the observer; stop clears pending reason as well."
    },
    {
      "area": "Accepted selection cancellation",
      "assessment": "requestArm(invalidate:true) invokes existing SelectionAuthority.cancel synchronously; exact IDs cancel only pending SelectionSubmissionQueue entries. Queue cancellation does not cancel the running consumer. Coordinator.cancelAcceptedSelections uses exact tokens and cancelPreparedIfNeeded, so an operation already at dispatchIntent or later is not rewritten as cancelled/pre-input or replayed. The unchanged Core drain retires selection authority after atomic dispatch intent before append; original operation, target and receipt remain immutable."
    },
    {
      "area": "In-flight capture and late publication",
      "assessment": "The scheduler preserves the original in-flight capture while changing epoch, rejects its stale acknowledgement, and issues a pending wake after completion. No target captured after the click is backdated or substituted. Ordinary chromeFocus leaves the epoch intact and only requests observation. This patch does not cancel an in-flight Apple Events capture merely to start another."
    },
    {
      "area": "In-flight input and original observation",
      "assessment": "The changed callback does not cancel watchedCompletions, originalRecoveryTask or an active adapter append/reconcile. Web adapter page validation, immutable operation/attempt/hash/target identity, Chrome kernel process lifetime guards, before-commit checks, pre-input rejection proof and UNKNOWN rules are byte-identical to base. A genuine window change can still cause an input-side original-target check to refuse; this is retained safety, not a reroute or a safe-retry grant."
    },
    {
      "area": "Retained uncertainty",
      "assessment": "AX notification delivery and one Task.yield remain asynchronous. This change shortens a known stale-ACK interval after a delivered structural hint and preserves hints during coalescing; it does not prove every window/tab transition is seen before a click or make a truly no-ACK click succeed. Title/focus rearm still relies on authoritative capture and input-time target checks. No stronger cold-first-click or physical claim is approved."
    }
